    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0354" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 871.0144/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-10">January 10,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Legation’s confidential
                    despatch No. 23, of the 9th instant, in regard to the situation in the Dobrudja,
                    I have the honor to enclose herewith a copy of a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >memoire</hi> presented to the Brigadier General commanding the British
                    forces of Silistra, signed by the Mayor of that town in the name of the
                    inhabitants.</p>
                <p>I would call attention to the fact that Silistra is the largest town in the
                    Southern or Bulgarian portion of the Dobrudja.</p>
                <pb facs="0355" n="267" xml:id="pg267"/>
                <p>A copy of this <hi rendition="#italic">memoire</hi> has been sent to me by the
                    Mayor of the town in a letter, copy of which is enclosed herewith,<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d186-f1"/> of which I have merely acknowledged the receipt.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles S. Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S. A copy of the above despatch has been forwarded to the American Peace
                        Mission, Paris.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d186-a1.xml" xpointer="d186-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
